       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Ben Pennell",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5bba58f3eb6f6e2ccfd097c6",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Regarding ocfl object sessions surviving reboots, that seems to also imply that fedora transactions would need to as well, since the hierarchy goes fedora tx -> persistence session -> object session. Is that something new we are committing to?",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I'm also trying to work out where the decision about whether to commit to the mutable head or a new version would happen. If autoversioning is repo wide, then it could probably happen almost anywhere. If it were to be an option per object, then it seems like a decision to make at the object level, which might imply that the OCFLObjectSession would figure this out rather than being told how to commit.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
